course: dictionary
lesson: 3948
title: Money words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Funding is a noun, a thing, and it means money given for a special purpose. The purpose is the key clue: the money is given to do a job, such as building a playground or paying for research. Read the words around it to find that purpose.
explain: «The school received funding for a new playground.» Received means got, and a new playground is the special purpose. So funding must be money the school was given to pay for the playground.
explain: «NASA's missions have been planned to visit Venus, though their dates and funding keep changing.» Dates and funding are named together, and things that keep changing can make a plan change too. Ask: what word would fit here? Money for the project. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Funding means money given for a special purpose.
fact: Money can come from a government, an organisation or a person.
fact: «Research needs funding» means scientists need money to pay for their experiments and tests.
fact: A good check is to swap "money given for a special purpose" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Funding is often shared between projects, so each project gets a part of the money.
exercise: «The school received funding for a new playground.» What is funding in this sentence? | A list of the people who work at the school | *Money given for a special purpose, such as a playground | A game played outdoors | A new school building that has been finished
exercise: «NASA's missions have been planned to visit Venus, though their dates and funding keep changing.» What might change if the funding changes? | *The plans, such as the dates of the missions | The name of the scientist | The number of planets in the sky | The colour of Venus
exercise: Scientists say «research needs funding». What does this tell you? | Research only happens in the summer | Research is cheap and needs no money | *Scientists need money to pay for their research | Funding is a type of experiment
test: A school has £500 of funding, shared equally between two projects. How much does each project get? | £200 | *£250 | £100 | £500
test: Which could give funding to a project? | A bus driver on a trip | *An organisation that wants the project to succeed | The weather forecast | A window
exam: A science team says, «Our project cannot go on without funding.» What does funding mean? | A map of the lab | A rest between tests | A type of experiment | *Money given to pay for the project
